hart#Regions_of_the_Z_Smith_chart"><span class="tocnumber">2.2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Regions of the <span>Z</span> Smith chart</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-3 tocsection-8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Circles_of_constant_normalised_resistance_and_constant_normalised_reactance"><span class="tocnumber">2.2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Circles of constant normalised resistance and constant normalised reactance</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-2 tocsection-9"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Practical_examples"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Practical examples</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2 tocsection-10"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Working_with_both_the_Z_Smith_chart_and_the_Y_Smith_charts"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Working with both the <i>Z</i> Smith chart and the <i>Y</i> Smith charts</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2 tocsection-11"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Choice_of_Smith_chart_type_and_component_type"><span class="tocnumber">2.5</span> <span class="toctext">Choice of Smith chart type and component type</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-12"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Using_the_Smith_chart_to_solve_conjugate_matching_problems_with_distributed_components"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Using the Smith chart to solve conjugate matching problems with distributed components</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-13"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Using_the_Smith_chart_to_analyze_lumped-element_circuits"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Using the Smith chart to analyze lumped-element circuits</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-14"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Variations_and_extensions"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Variations and extensions</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2 tocsection-15"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#The_Y_Smith_chart"><span class="tocnumber">5.1</span> <span class="toctext">The <span>Y</span> Smith chart</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2 tocsection-16"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Extension_for_negative_resistance_(Real_part_of_z_%3C_0)"><span class="tocnumber">5.2</span> <span class="toctext">Extension for negative resistance (Real part of <span>z</span> &lt; 0)</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2 tocsection-17"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Mapping_of_the_Smith_chart_onto_a_unit_sphere"><span class="tocnumber">5.3</span> <span class="toctext">Mapping of the Smith chart onto a unit sphere</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-18"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#See_also"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">See also</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-19"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Footnotes"><span class="tocnumber">7</span> <span class="toctext">Footnotes</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-20"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#References"><span class="tocnumber">8</span> <span class="toctext">References</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-21"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#Further_reading"><span class="tocnumber">9</span> <span class="toctext">Further reading</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-22"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_chart#External_links"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">External links</span></a></li></ul></div></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mw4g" aria-labelledby="Overview"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 mf-collapsible-heading" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-controls="" aria-expanded="true"><span class="mf-icon mf-icon--small mf-collapsible-icon mf-icon-collapse" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="Overview">Overview</h2><span class="mw-editsection">
<a role="button" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Smith_chart&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Overview" class="cdx-button cdx-button--size-large cdx-button--fake-button cdx-button--fake-button--enabled cdx-button--icon-only cdx-button--weight-quiet ">
    <span class="minerva-icon minerva-icon--edit"></span>
<span>edit</span>
</a>

</span>

</div><div class="mf-collapsible-content">
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mw4w"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NetworkAnalyzer.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mw5A"><img resource="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NetworkAnalyzer.jpg" src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/NetworkAnalyzer.jpg/500px-NetworkAnalyzer.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="1490" data-file-height="1094" data-file-type="bitmap" height="294" width="400" class="mw-file-element" id="mw5Q" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption id="mw5g">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_analyzer_(electrical)" title="Network analyzer (electrical)" id="mw5w">network analyzer</a> set up to display measured data on a Smith chart.</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mw6A">The Smith chart is a mathematical transformation of the two-dimensional Cartesian complex plane. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_numbers" title="Complex numbers" class="mw-redirect" id="mw6Q">Complex numbers</a> with positive real parts map inside the circle. Those with negative real parts map outside the circle.
If we are dealing only with impedances with non-negative resistive components, our interest is focused on the area inside the circle. The transformation, for an impedance Smith chart, is:</p>

<p id="mw6g"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt80" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;math&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;display&quot;:&quot;block&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\\Gamma = \\frac{Z - Z_0}{Z + Z_0} = \\frac{z - 1}{z + 1},&quot;}}" id="mw6w"><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle \Gamma ={\frac {Z-Z_{0}}{Z+Z_{0}}}={\frac {z-1}{z+1}},}">
  <semantics>
