<p id="mwATo">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_system_of_units" title="International system of units" class="mw-redirect" id="mwATs">SI unit</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrical_impedance" title="Electrical impedance" id="mwATw">impedance</a> is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohm" title="Ohm" id="mwAT0">ohm</a> with the symbol of the upper case <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_alphabet" title="Greek alphabet" id="mwAT4">Greek letter</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omega" title="Omega" id="mwAT8">omega</a> (Î©) and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SI_unit" title="SI unit" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAUA">SI unit</a> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Admittance" title="Admittance" id="mwAUE">admittance</a> is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siemens_(unit)" title="Siemens (unit)" id="mwAUI">siemens</a> with the symbol of an upper case letter S. Normalised impedance and normalised admittance are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimensionless" title="Dimensionless" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAUM">dimensionless</a>. Actual impedances and admittances must be normalised before using them on a Smith chart. Once the result is obtained it may be de-normalised to obtain the actual result.</p>

